-- Part V, the table of injury rates (V. BẢNG TỈ LỆ THƯƠNG TẬT), lines 686-878 of the
-- source, and the six principles for paying under it.
-- Benefits 1 and 3 pay partial permanent injury "according to the table"; each rate is a
-- percentage of the sum insured of the benefit claimed.
--
-- THE DATA IS GENERATED. `the table of injury rates` was written by a script from the raw
-- text: one printed line with a rate becomes one row, its `-- src:` lines are quoted from
-- the file, and its two figures are read off the line by a regular expression, never
-- retyped. The per-row tests in pti268-tests-table.l4 were generated from the same lines
-- by a different reading of the figures, so the two can disagree.
--
-- Section I (death) prints no item number; it is item 0 here.
-- Items 76, 77 and 78 print "Dưới 55 tuổi" and "Trên 55 tuổi", or "Dưới 45" and "Trên 45":
-- an insured aged exactly 55 or 45 falls in neither sub-row. The rows are kept as printed;
-- choosing a sub-row is the assessor's input (finding X14). Item 48 prints "Ít nhất 5 cm" and
-- "Từ 3 đến 5 cm": exactly 5 cm falls in both (finding X14).

